Subject: Cantor Public Procedure Schema Direction Profile Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 9ff8c14e-7855-42a1-ac6c-052f0eb197ab

& [Selected] is isolated direction-qualified definition universes
  + follows the pinned library contract boundary
  + preserves one semantic type identity while preventing unsafe transport substitution
  + leaves ordinary local JSON Pointer names stable inside each document
  + makes current cross-direction equality measurable without turning it into authority

& [RejectedSingleMap] would conflate contracts
  + stable type names are not sufficient cache keys when contract changes schema identity
  + crossing types could inherit whichever direction happened to generate first

& [RejectedDirectionInPointerKey] adds avoidable encoding risk
  + distinct bundle maps already carry direction
  + document-local references can retain stable type names and simple closure validation

& [Safety] comes from explicit identity
  + direction-first generation, isolated caches, domain-separated fingerprints, dual crossing-type proof, and same-direction compatibility

